<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Rationalising a binomial denominator of the form c - sqrt(b) using its conjugate</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Rationalise the denominator of the following expression by multiplying by its conjugate, giving your answer in simplest form. <i>(Note: For example, write <code>(3*(5+sqrt(17)))/8</code> to represent \(\dfrac{3(5+\sqrt{17})}{8}\).)</i></p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ \frac{{@p@}}{{@c@} - \sqrt{{@b@}}} \]</p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate \({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}}{{@c@} - \sqrt{{@b@}}} \times \frac{{@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}}}{{@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}}} = \frac{{@p@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{({@c@} - \sqrt{{@b@}})({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Simplify the denominator using the difference of two squares \((x - y)(x + y) = x^2 - y^2\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle ({@c@} - \sqrt{{@b@}})({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}}) = {@c@}^2 - (\sqrt{{@b@}})^2 = {@c2@} - {@b@} = {@d@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Substituting this back into the fraction gives:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{{@d@}}\)</p>

[[ if test="g = 1" ]]
<p><b>Step 3: Check for common factors</b><br>
Since \({@p@}\) and \({@d@}\) have no common factor other than \(1\), the fraction is already in simplest form:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{{@d@}}\)</p>
[[ elif test="d_red = 1" ]]
<p><b>Step 3: Divide by the common factor of \({@g@}\)</b><br>
Since \({@p@} \div {@d@} = {@p_red@}\), dividing the numerator and denominator by \({@g@}\) simplifies the fraction completely:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{{@d@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
[[ else ]]
<p><b>Step 3: Cancel the common factor of \({@g@}\)</b><br>
Both \({@p@}\) and \({@d@}\) share a common factor of \({@g@}\) (\({@p@} \div {@g@} = {@p_red@}\) and \({@d@} \div {@g@} = {@d_red@}\)). Cancelling \({@g@}\) gives:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@p@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{{@d@}} = \frac{{@p_red@}({@c@} + \sqrt{{@b@}})}{{@d_red@}}\)</p>
[[/ if ]]

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@p@}}{{@c@} - \sqrt{{@b@}}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
